      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If they aren't visible pests, you might be dealing with mold spores or perhaps fermentation byproducts that are starting in a hidden spot. Mold can be incredibly subtle, starting as a faint discoloration or a strange texture that looks like a tiny clump. It’s a good idea to inspect all your equipment—pots, stirring spoons, and even the rims of the jars—for any microscopic residue or slight dampness. A little bit of moisture in a dark corner can be a breeding ground for things that are nearly invisible at first glance.",
